body:
Slice 5 of 7 of #636. Depends on #657 and #653 (the staged-publication committer, scheduled immediately before this slice).

## What

- Complete: fingerprinted (a Complete reusing an upload id with a different part list is a different operation), session-fenced publication through #653's committer (`require(mpu == Completing@E)` passed in as the parameterized precondition), the published version computed from the re-read prior at each flip attempt;
- segmented map production — the first real producer of `ChunkMap::Segmented`;
- the ETag recorded in the `Completed` session record, so a retried identical Complete inside the tombstone window answers the recorded value;
- the attempts budget must not wedge an `Open` session: in the discontinued patch, three malformed Completes made the fourth, correct one answer `CompleteAttemptsExhausted` with the session still `Open` and every part durable — Abort-and-full-reupload as the only exit, contradicting the patch's own docs ("a client's typo never wedges an upload");
- subset-Complete evidence: unnamed parts' fragments are `orphan:`-marked before their naming record disappears, and no published fragment is orphan-marked.

## Acceptance

- parts staged out of order (at least one non-final part not a whole multiple of the chunk size) read back byte-identical after Complete; the ETag equals the pure function of the recorded digests;
- typo-then-correct Complete succeeds; fingerprint mismatch and tombstone-window retry answer per the decision-3 table;
- `cargo xtask ci` green.

Part of #636 / #508 / epic #513.
